Command: ipc_bench 20000
Secure IPC samples (ms): 778, 746, 737, 746, 727
Sorted samples (ms): 727, 737, 746, 746, 778
Secure IPC median: 746 ms
Original baseline median: 647 ms
Observed difference: +99 ms, +15.3%, +4950 ns/iteration
Per-run workload: 20,000 × pipe → close(read) → close(write)

Interpretation:
- Quota limits reject excess resources with EMFILE or ENOSPC and recover after close.
- A pipe creation that cannot reserve two total FD slots returns EMFILE; after
  one descriptor is closed, pipe creation succeeds, proving no counter leak.
- The QEMU timing comparison is an end-to-end observation across dates. It
  supports a constant-factor overhead conclusion, not a hardware-precise claim.
